WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.568
-Tariq and I are
about to do something fun.

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:05.005
It's time for the first annual
"Tonight Show" Pizza-Off.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.439
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:09.675
The rules are simple.

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:11.510
The rules were
make any pizza you want,

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.713
and whoever makes the most
delicious pizza possible

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.881
is the winner
and gets their name engraved

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:18.985
on the "Tonight Show" Pizza-Off
Golden Pizza Slicer.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:24.657
Look at this thing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.425
Our judge has
soundproof headphones, right?

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.728
He's not watching?
So, Tariq and I, earlier,

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.797
we made our pizzas,
and we recorded the whole thing.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.031
I have no idea what Tariq
is gonna make.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.399
He has no idea
what I'm going to make.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.067
Check it out.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.569 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.671
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:42.241 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:45.178
Hey, guys, it's Jimmy.
You may recognize me as

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.780
the "Tonight Show"
Burger-Off champion.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.816 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.684
-You guys!
-Number one!

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.586
The number one burger!
-I love you!

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.054
I love you!

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.456
But, yeah, I guess I won.
No big deal.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.358
I don't want to gloat
or brag that I won.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.794
-Hey, what's up?
Tariq Trotter here.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:03.796
I been hearing about how Jimmy's
running around New York City.

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.564
He's got his trophy
on a necklace.

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:07.667
You know what I mean?
He's bragging and boasting.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.235
-You know, now that I've won,

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.538
I feel like
I have a legacy to protect.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:12.838
-I'm here to shut that down.

00:01:12.838 --> 00:01:16.942
Today, I'm gonna be making
my Pie'ing Lotus Pizza.

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:20.513
Turkey pepperoni,
fresh mozzarella, sauce,

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:23.416
and I'm gonna finish it off
with some hot honey.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.918
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:29.288
-I'm a trend-sniffer.
And I sniff out trends.

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:31.023
I feel like there's big trend

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:33.293
with carb on carb
happening right now.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:36.929
So I went with spaghetti
and meatballs on a pizza.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:38.431 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.233
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.168
First of all,
you start with the dough.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.371
You can either make it yourself,
or I go to my local pizzeria

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.140
and just buy dough from them.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.474
And just stretch it around.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:51.811
-I'm terrible with, like,
stretching out a pizza dough.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.479
It's never been my jam.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:56.916
It's got a hole in it now.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.651
Okay.
We got another dough?

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.985
-A lot of people say
the trick to making

00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:03.523
a good pizza dough is height.
[ Grunts ]

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:06.258
Don't worry about the holes.
No one can even see the holes.

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:09.362
The new "Halloween" movie
is in theaters October 31st.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.297
Check it out.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:15.000
-I did borrow a little bit from
my days working in Pizzeria Uno,

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.137
in that I put the pepperoni on
before I put the cheese.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:21.440
-I get my sauce
from a can called Bianco.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.942
And what you do is,
you use your hands

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.811
to just squeeze the tomatoes
and make the sauce.

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:28.147
Just get any, like,
kind of aggression out.

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:30.516
[ Grunting ]

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:33.886
[ Record needle scratching ]

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:36.055
-Got to do that before you
put it in the often.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.856
This is
the rock-a-bye technique.

00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:41.060
Rock-a-bye pizza,
because Jimmy's going to sleep.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.962
Going night-night.
You ready to go night-night?!

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.564
-Into the pizza oven it goes.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.999
And then you kind of
want to go, like -- "Shww!"

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:50.035
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:52.839
-And...it's not working.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:56.308
The pizza's
not coming off the peel.

00:02:56.308 --> 00:02:58.711
-But I do want to -- ooh.
Gosh, that almost fell.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.213
Gah!
Ooh!

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.814
What it would mean for me
to have my name

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.950
engraved in the pizza trophy?

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:07.820
I'd be on cloud nine, or as
they say in Italy...

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:11.490
cloud niño.
Nino?

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.692
Ninto?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.628
-To have my name engraved
on the "Tonight Show"

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:18.831
Golden Pizza Slicer,
it wouldn't matter to me at all.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.032
Who cares?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.935
All right.
So, I'm about to take it out.

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.270
It's not bad.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.238
-All right,
now we want to get our pasta.

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:27.373
You can take
a couple of meatballs

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.975
and make them into smaller bits.

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.542
I don't know what Tariq
has on his pizza,

00:03:30.542 --> 00:03:33.379
but I know what
he doesn't have -- meat bits.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.380
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:38.083 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:40.619
-Secret weapon -- I'mma hit it
with a little spicy honey,

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:41.721
give it a little kick.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.257
-Banana peppers.
Now this is when I win.

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.158
That's what I'm talking about.
Boom.

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:48.494
-And I feel like I used
to have beef with Jimmy,

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:51.063
but now, you know,
it's evolved into pepperoni.

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:53.399
There we go.
Done.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.301
It's level.
-See, you need good ingredients.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.571
Yes, you need a good pizza oven,
but you also you need respect.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:01.274
And this pizza
was made with respect.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:02.775
-I'm not even gonna
trash talk you, Jimmy.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.244
I'm just gonna let
the taste do the talking.

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:10.249
-I think I won again with the
spaghetti-and-meatball pizza.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:13.486
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.487
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:17.556
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:04:17.556 --> 00:04:18.824
-Wow!
-Wow!

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:20.459
-Wow!
Interesting.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:22.095
All right,
to decide the wining pizza,

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.864
we have a special guest serving
as our master pizza judge.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.599
He's founder
of Scott's Pizza Tours,

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:30.503
runs a pizza-themed non-profit,
Slice Out Hunger,

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.238
and holds
the Guinness world record

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:34.640
for largest collection
of pizza boxes.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.776
Please welcome Scott Wiener!

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:38.277
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:42.782 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.817
-Welcome to the show.
Thank you, Scott.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.819
I wasn't doing that --
-Whatev.

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.454
-I wasn't doing that to --
-Okay, okay.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.656
-I didn't do this
after I saw Scott.

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:51.724
-Got it, yep.
-Quick little fist bump.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.059
That's all.
-Yep.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.293
-Thanks for being here.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:56.128
I appreciate you
coming to the show.

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:59.565
I love your videos, your work.
I also love your book.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.934
And you have the world's largest
collection of pizza boxes.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.670
-I do, it's true.
-Did that start recently or no?

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.172
-No, man.
Like 12 years ago,

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:08.107
I started collecting pizza boxes

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.776
and noticed that
they're not all the same.

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:11.778
And, you know,
they're pieces of art, you know?

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:14.546
When they have a pizza in them,
pizza box.

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:16.349
When they're flipped vertical,
art.

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:18.417
-Art. I agree, Scott.
That's awesome.

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:19.552
-Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:21.086
-It's now time
to try the pizza.

00:05:21.086 --> 00:05:24.156
Okay. Whenever you're ready,
please try pizza number one.

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:27.025
Numero uno.
-All right.

00:05:27.025 --> 00:05:28.194
Lets see what's going on.

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:31.597
Oh.
Interesting. Whoa.

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:32.899
There's spaghetti on this.

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:34.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.502
This is not a mistake?
This is actually...?

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:37.870
-That's a good question.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.872
-Actually -- All right.
All right.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:43.009
I love pepperoncini,
so I'm excited about this.

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.478
This actually
looks like a serious dough.

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:47.512
Great fermentation
from the edge.

00:05:47.512 --> 00:05:50.416
Some nice open-crumb structure,
which I always look for.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:53.619
On the bottom, I see a really,
really good bake, you know.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.187
Things I'm looking for.

00:05:55.187 --> 00:06:02.361 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:04.029
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:07.032
That was -- salt.

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:08.301
-You got some salt there.
-Somebody got a little

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:10.235
carried away with the salt.
-Yep, too much, yep.

00:06:10.235 --> 00:06:12.104
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:16.075
Well, I got to say, decent pie.

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:18.077
-All right.
Decent pie -- not bad.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.378
-Decent pie.
-Yeah.

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:22.314
-That pie was decent.
-Yep, I agree with him.

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:24.750
-Number two.
-Yup, number two is right.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.286
-Oh! Okay.

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:30.122
Here's what I'm seeing on both
of these -- post-oven basil.

00:06:30.122 --> 00:06:32.024
I appreciate that.
-Mm.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:34.260
-Oh, there's honey on this.
-Ooh, yeah.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:37.329
-There's honey.
Super common right now --

00:06:37.329 --> 00:06:39.998
hot honey
with a pork product on top.

00:06:39.998 --> 00:06:41.567
I'm lovin' this.
-Pretty common, yeah.

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:46.638
-Yeah. A little derivative,
but, you know...

00:06:46.638 --> 00:06:50.209
These are --
These are both legit pizzas.

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:52.111
So...

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.946
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.448
Honestly, no offense, guys,

00:06:56.448 --> 00:06:59.018
I expected a disaster
from at least one of these.

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:01.453
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.453 --> 00:07:03.689
-You take offense.
That's a compliment for me.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.558
-Yes.
Yeah, I concur.

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:07.592
-This is great.
Now, Scott, the moment of truth.

00:07:07.592 --> 00:07:09.728
Please write down your choice
for the winning pizza

00:07:09.728 --> 00:07:11.297
and put into the official

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:13.599
"Tonight Show" Pizza-Off
ballot box.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:18.771
Will it be pizza number one
or pizza number two?

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:21.507
You can only choose one.

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:23.108
-All right.
-And to make sure your vote

00:07:23.108 --> 00:07:25.578
is complete and secure,
Scott, please lock it

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.713
in the ballot box.
Just put it in there, yes.

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:30.783
And then, now please fasten
the straitjacket around the box.

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.618
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.520
-You're gonna drop it into
a pool of water, too?

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.821
-Well, finally,
the shark-proof cage.

00:07:35.821 --> 00:07:37.256
-Ah.
-We do actually have

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:39.458
a shark-proof cage,
just to make sure.

00:07:39.458 --> 00:07:41.494
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:43.262
We know the vote's in there.

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:45.031
Can't be tampered with.

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:47.500
Now that the vote
is securely locked in,

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.302
we can reveal to Scott
who made what.

00:07:50.302 --> 00:07:51.871
[ Clears throat ]
Do you want to go first?

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:55.341
-Um, I made the pizza
that you assumed was, you know,

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:57.577
the derivative pork product pie.

00:07:57.577 --> 00:07:59.812
But I made it
with turkey pepperoni,

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:02.781
which I've never seen
in any pizza place on Earth.

00:08:02.781 --> 00:08:04.249
So...
-Maybe a reason.

00:08:04.249 --> 00:08:05.718
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:06.952
I went with the --

00:08:06.952 --> 00:08:09.088
See, I think the honey trend
has come and gone.

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:10.389
[ Laughter ]

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:13.259
I believe that carb on carb
is the future.

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:16.262
And I went with double carb.
People are running marathons,

00:08:16.262 --> 00:08:17.930
people out there,
they need some stuff.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.132
I'm here to help you.
-Interesting.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:22.000
-So, Scott,
now can you please remove

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.103
the shark-proof cage
and the straitjacket

00:08:25.103 --> 00:08:27.106
from the ballot box.
In fact, I don't even know

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:28.741
if you need -- you can probably
just open the top.

00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:31.610
I don't even think it's locked.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:32.711
You can just open it.
Yeah.

00:08:32.711 --> 00:08:33.745
-It's not really that secure,
huh?

00:08:33.745 --> 00:08:35.380
-No, not really.
-All right, all right.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.082
Okay. Let's see.
-Ooh, gosh.

00:08:37.082 --> 00:08:39.652
Oh, my goodness.
I just want to tell my --

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:40.986
-Ah, ba-ba-ba, deh deh!

00:08:40.986 --> 00:08:42.988
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:42.988 --> 00:08:47.960 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:52.030
We back, baby!
We back, baby!

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:55.434
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:57.770
-Go to bed!
Honey, if you're watching,

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.006
put the kids to bed!
They don't need to see this.

00:09:00.006 --> 00:09:01.741
The kids don't need to see this!

00:09:01.741 --> 00:09:04.009
Congratulations to the champion,
Tariq Trotter!

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:05.444
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:08.380
And, again,
thank you to Scott Wiener,

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:10.516
our pizza expert!

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:12.117
Thank you for being here, bud.
I appreciate it.

00:09:12.117 --> 00:09:14.453
-We'll be right back
with Jeff Daniels, everybody.

00:09:14.453 --> 00:09:16.355
Come on back.

00:09:16.355 --> 00:09:18.157
I put too much salt on it?

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:20.159
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:25.197 line:0%
♪♪

